local.properties
.gradle/
build/
*.iml
.idea/

# Parity artifacts pulled off a device are run outputs, not source. The golden
# host report IS committed (see parity/), because the gate compares against it.
parity/device_report*.json

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Signing material. The upload key and its passwords never live in the repo:
# a leaked upload key has to be reset with Google, and a keystore committed
# next to the source it signs is not a key, it is a shared secret.
keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# Calibration data is never redistributed from here. A patched bin belongs to a
# specific car and the switch-patch XDF is third-party; both were committed
# under parity/fixtures/ until this repo went public (2026-08-20), and both were
# purged from history rather than just deleted. Supply them locally and point
# BOOST_FIXTURE_DIR at them — see parity/push_fixtures_and_compare.sh.
*.bin
*.xdf
parity/fixtures/

# Store screenshots are frames of a real session, so they show a real car's
# calibration — the boost panels are this car's target curves and the Changes
# panel names a real edit. They were held out of this public repo until that was
# a deliberate decision rather than a side effect of `git add -A`; the decision
# was made on 2026-09-08 (RELEASE_CHECKLIST item 33) and they are now tracked,
# because a live Play listing publishes them anyway and having them here keeps
# them versioned alongside the scripts that compose them:
#   python3 store/make_screenshots.py     (store/captures/ -> store/graphics/screenshots/)
